<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Innioasis Updater CE Notice Feed Markup Specification
  Hosted at: https://innioasis.app/notice.xml

  Displays on-screen hint toast announcements to users of the app.

  The app shows ONE notice at a time on the Select Software card: the notice
  that best matches what the reader is looking at (the selected model, its
  hardware revision, and the firmware repository and release tag they picked)
  or a device they logged for update reminders. Several applicable notices
  take turns on that card, so they can be read without opening the list.
  The Notices page, the pop-out list and the notification tray always show
  EVERY active notice (with no contextual narrowing): an announcement for
  everyone is never hidden by the current selection.

  Fields:
  - id: required, unique string identifier for the notice.
  - persistent: boolean ("true" | "false", default: "false").
      * "false" (or omitted): Non-persistent notice. When dismissed by the user,
        it is permanently dismissed and will not return on the next app run.
      * "true": Persistent notice. It will return on every app launch, even if
        dismissed during a prior run.
      * DISMISSALS FOLLOW NOTICES, NOT THE FILE: a dismissal is remembered per
        notice id. If the feed changes, any notice with an id the user has not
        dismissed appears, while dismissed notices stay hidden even when the
        rest of the file changes. New ids are the only way to bring a notice
        back after dismissal (persistent="true" returns every launch).
  - severity: "info" | "warning" | "critical" (default: "info").
  - type: optional release marker: "player_update" or "app_update". It
      selects the notification category; omitted means an ordinary notice.
  - from: optional posting date or timestamp. Accepts YYYY-MM-DD, or a timestamp
      YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM (also YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS, or a space instead of the T).
      The app shows this on the notice as "Posted ...". Shown on or after it.
  - until: optional ISO date YYYY-MM-DD. Shown on or before this date. Not shown to users.
  - platform: optional comma-separated list of platforms ("mac,windows,linux").
      Omitted means every platform.

  Contextual targeting (all optional; every field that is set must match):
  - models: comma-separated target models (e.g. "Y1,Y2"). Omit for all models.
  - device_type: comma-separated hardware revisions, e.g. "A" or "B" (also
      accepts "Type A"). Only Y1 currently ships more than one revision. A
      notice with a revision is not offered for a model that has no revisions.
  - firmware_repo: the GitHub repository the notice is about, written exactly
      as in slidia_manifest.xml, e.g. "rockbox-y1/rockbox". A full GitHub URL
      is accepted and compared case-insensitively. Wildcards are allowed
      ("spycemagic/*"). The notice is offered when the reader has selected a
      firmware from that repository, or has a device logged for update
      reminders whose software comes from it.
  - firmware_version: comma-separated release tag(s) the notice is about,
      e.g. "v3.2.0", "v3.2.*" or "*". "*" means any release of the named
      repository. A leading "v" is optional, so "3.2.0" matches a v3.2.0 tag.
      The notice is offered when the reader has selected that release, or has
      logged a device whose last recorded install is that release.
  - A notice with none of these attributes is for EVERYONE: it is always on
      the card's rotation, whatever the selection, and always in every list.

  How the attributes combine (contextual card only):
    model AND device_type AND firmware_repo AND firmware_version (when set)
    must all agree with one reader context. A reader has several contexts:
    the current Select Software selection, plus one for each device logged for
    update reminders (Settings -> Player Update Reminders, or an install).
    A notice is offered if it matches ANY of those contexts. Notices are
    ordered on the card by specificity: firmware_repo, then
    firmware_version, then device_type, then models, then everyone.

  Child elements:
  - <title>: required, headline of the notice.
  - <content>: required, description/body text (also supports <body>).
  - <full_content>: optional full body, written in Markdown. Rendered in the
      app's full notice view (not on the banner or card, which use <content>),
      and on the notice's own page on the site. Supports headings, lists,
      emphasis, code, block quotes, links and images. It may also be supplied as
      a full_content="..." attribute on <notice>.
  - <url>: optional URL behind the full notice's Open page button. Omit it to
      show no link; a URL that is only the bare site root is ignored too. The
      app opens the full Markdown view locally before offering this page.
  - <link>: accepted as an alias for <url>.
-->
<notices updated="2026-11-03">

  <!-- Everyone: no targeting at all. Always on the card, always in the list. -->
  <notice id="2026-10-20-psa-usb" persistent="true" severity="warning" from="2026-10-20T08:00" until="2026-11-20">
    <title>Use a direct USB port</title>
    <content>Avoid USB hubs during an install. Some hubs drop the connection partway through.</content>
  </notice>

  <!-- One model, one hardware revision, one repository: a Y1 Type A warning
       about Rockbox that appears when Rockbox (from rockbox-y1/rockbox) is
       selected for that device, or when a Y1 Type A player whose last install
       was Rockbox is logged for update reminders. -->
  <notice id="2026-11-03-rockbox-y1-typea" persistent="false" severity="warning" from="2026-11-03" until="2026-12-31" models="Y1" device_type="A" firmware_repo="rockbox-y1/rockbox" firmware_version="*">
    <title>Rockbox on Y1 Type A: check your build</title>
    <content>Builds before 0.5 do not run on Type A units sold after March 2026. Update to 0.5 or later before installing.</content>
    <full_content>Type A Y1 units sold after March 2026 ship with a bootloader that rejects older Rockbox builds.

- **Rockbox 0.5 or later** is required on those units.
- Older builds stop at the boot logo instead of starting.

If the player does not start after an install, restore Original Software with Updater CE and install a current Rockbox build.</full_content>
    <url>https://innioasis.app/notices.html?notice=2026-11-03-rockbox-y1-typea</url>
  </notice>

  <!-- One release of one repository: shown when that exact tag is selected, or
       when a logged device's last install was that tag. -->
  <notice id="2026-11-04-rockbox-y2-3-2-1" persistent="false" severity="info" from="2026-11-04" until="2026-12-31" models="Y2" firmware_repo="spycemagic/y2-rockbox" firmware_version="v3.2.1">
    <title>Rockbox 3.2.1 for Y2: known issues</title>
    <content>360p themes and MicroSD libraries are still being worked on in this release. Original Software remains the safe choice if you rely on a MicroSD library.</content>
    <full_content>The community has reported two open problems with Rockbox 3.2.1 on Y2:

- **360p themes do not apply.** The player keeps showing the stock artwork.
- **Music on a MicroSD card is not listed** after the install.

Staying on Original Software avoids both. Restoring is one run of Updater CE; music on the MicroSD card is left alone, but music in the Y2's internal storage is erased.</full_content>
  </notice>

  <!-- A model the reader may not have selected: still offered when that model is
       logged for update reminders. -->
  <notice id="2026-10-25-firmware-advisory" persistent="false" severity="info" from="2026-10-25" until="2026-12-31" models="Y1,Y2">
    <title>Original Software 3.2.1 Available</title>
    <content>An updated firmware release for Y1 and Y2 players is now available in the community catalogue.</content>
  </notice>

</notices>
